    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a7">

                <pb facs="0355" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg331"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            de Kotzebue.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 42.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the copy of the complaint of Capt. G. I. Dahlberg, of the Russian bark <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hans</hi>, alleging that in contravention of his treaty
                    rights he was arrested and imprisoned on a warrant in a civil case, issued by
                    the United States district court for the southern district of Mississippi, the
                    action having been instituted by a member of the crew against the commander of
                    the vessel.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that I have submitted the matter to the
                    Attorney-General for his examination.</p>
                <p>In compliance with your oral request, I return the copy of the complaint left by
                    you at the Department.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Inclosure: Complaint of Capt. G. I. Dahlberg.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
